# Climate country wiring (no app.js)

## Do this

When a yield/reference country is ready for the dashboard:

```bash
cd "New for anti/scripts/yield_model"
python3 scaffold_manifest.py {country}
# Fill TODOs: iso, label_ko, label_en, view, sources (and any [TODO,TODO] coords)
python3 build_registry.py --check
```

Then PR **only**:

- `scripts/yield_model/{country}/model.yaml` (+ package if new)
- `public/data/{country}_yield_forecast.json` (if not already on main)

**Do not** edit `New for anti/app.js` / `CLIMATE_COUNTRIES` to add a country.  
**Do not** commit `public/data/climate_registry_v1.json` (generated on main by CI).

Spec: `scripts/yield_model/MODEL_MANIFEST.md`

## Why

Parallel country work used to collide on one `app.js` object. Manifests isolate each country; the UI fetches the registry.

## Orphan forecasts

If `--check` fails with “예측 JSON 이 있는데 매니페스트가 없다”, scaffold that country (or a thin `model.yaml` folder) before merging — otherwise CI blocks everyone.
